    "reasoning": "All 16 final answers agree with the mathematics and their respective captured worked solutions. Two source defects do not change the answers: q-39648 replaces the exact 0.001/64=0.000015625 with 0.000016 during its inequality calculation; the exact threshold still lies between 39 and 40. q-210773 concludes with b=1 although the parameter is a. Mathematics by question: q-103837 integrates the polar speed 4\\cos(\\theta/2) over [0,\\pi], giving 8. q-9532 has constant polar speed 2 over an interval of width \\pi/3, giving 2\\pi/3. q-87862 compares a strictly negative number with a strictly positive number, so every real x works. q-49387 uses x\\,dx=du/2 and x^2=u-1. q-49532 uses x\\,dx=-du/4, x^2=(3-u)/2, and bounds 1 and 3. q-85673 selects the concave-down graph, whose chords lie below the curve. q-116621 gives 30(9)+50(7)+40(9)=980. q-78297 preserves x and negates y. q-104195 maximizes x(7.5-x) at x=3.75, giving 14.0625 square meters, rounded to 14.06. q-82704 approaches the singular upper endpoint -3 from the left. q-141181 similarly approaches 2 from the left; this improper integral diverges, but the selected limit is its correct definition. q-39648 has a_n=64(3/4)^{n-1}; a_39 exceeds 0.001 and a_40 is below it. q-210773 minimizes 10a^2-20a+20 at a=1. q-87502 imposes y=1-x and minimizes 2x^2+2 at (0,1). q-117463 imposes y=7/2 and minimizes (x-6)^2 at x=6. q-118389 has squared distance x^2-3x+1/x+6, whose derivative is 2x-3-1/x^2. No submitted grade or earlier answer is supplied; all MA evidence below comes from the question's own captured worked solution.",
